I've left #49 open and labelled it `needs-decision`. The fix is complete, but I can't verify the apply, which is the issue's condition for closing.

- **What's done:** all four commits of the fix are on main (580d4ca, c9dc2bc, c6e2899, 8e92ac8). The last land ran the full gates and the build came back green (tacplus-dev/build pipeline 3061635722).
- **What I couldn't check:**
  - whether `apply:ci` of the pinned commit succeeded;
  - whether `runner-build-region` exists and the old zonal `runner-build` is gone;
  - whether `runner-reap` is running on the manager.

  This runner has no Google Cloud credentials, cloud's pipeline isn't publicly visible, and GitHub shows no apply status for those commits.
- **What I did:** commented on #49 asking the hub to either close it once those three are confirmed, or paste the results and remove the label so the next run closes it. I recommended closing it themselves, since only the infrastructure check is left. The label stops the looper from starting this issue again just to wait.
- **Commits:** none this run; there was nothing to change.
- **Checkpoint:** I wrote one recording this state. Its push reported "2 files changed, 246 insertions" even though the checkout had no changes when I started, and I didn't check which files those were.
